{
    "background_story": "Jayce was a fierce and fearless college basketball player, earning the nickname 'Gamecock' for his tenacious defense and lightning-quick reflexes on the court. Hailing from a small town in South Carolina, Jayce led his high school team to a state championship before being recruited by the University of South Carolina. As a Gamecock, he became a fan favorite, known for his clutch three-pointers and ability to shut down opponents' top scorers. Jayce's passion and work ethic inspired his teammates, and together they made a deep run in the NCAA tournament. Off the court, Jayce was a humble and kind soul, often visiting local schools and hospitals to spread joy and promote the importance of education. His legacy as a Gamecock continued to inspire future generations of basketball players and fans alike.",
